Z||000037||AutoXdbdragSE||11-28-2001||01:13 AM||||This work for ya?<BR>CPU: Hitachi SH-4<BR>200 MHz clock rate<BR>360 MIPS (Millions of Instructions Per Second)<BR>1.4 GigaFLOPS (Floating-point Operations Per Second<BR>128-bit 3D calculations<BR>64-bit data bus<BR>800+ MBytes/second bus bandwidth<P>it does video at 128 bit, but it is only a 64 bit processor.. my point is that the PS2 is a techincaly a TRUE 128bit system. everything on it runs at 128bits or higher nothing is less.. ecept sound.. but sound doesn't really matter. because it's at least 32 bit.. i'm not sure if it's higher.. 32bit sound is pretty good<P>PS2<BR>CPU: 128-bit "Emotion Engine"<BR>300 MHz clock rate<BR>6.2 GigaFLOPS (Floating-point Operation Per Second)<BR>3.2 GBytes/second bus bandwidth<BR>66 million polygons/second peak rendering rate<P>Graphics Core: "Graphics Synthesizer"<BR>150 MHz clock rate<BR>Compressed Image Decoder: MPEG2<BR>DRAM Bus bandwidth: 48 GBytes/second<BR>DRAM Bus width: 320 MBytes/second<P>both sets of sheets from gamersutopia<P>so your dreamcast is beter than the ps2, just like that amd K6-2w/3d now is as fast as my athlon thunderbird 1.33.. ||||reg||1
